---
description: Feature folders in Next.js apps — no cross-feature imports
globs: apps/*/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Feature modules

- `app/` and `src/proxy.ts` — composition roots. Import `@/features/<name>`.
- `features/<name>/` — one domain. Add `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, `server/queries/`, `server/actions/` as needed. Relative imports inside the feature — not `@/features/<this-feature>/...`. Never import another feature. Orchestration (why/when: policy, auth, state) stays here.
- `shared/` — this app only; never import a feature. Hoist a mechanic here when a **second** feature needs the same how.
- Cross-app libraries go in `packages/`. Do not put journey policy in a package.
- `src/lib` and `src/components` at the app root are not composition roots. Put that code in `shared/` or a feature.
